    "oralbiome_faq_KxQ7m3": {
      "type": "oralbiome-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_jjyJEw": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "How do I use OralBiome Pro?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I use OralBiome Pro?",
            "answer": "<p>After brushing and flossing, place one lozenge on your tongue and let it dissolve slowly. Do not chew. Avoid eating or drinking for 30 minutes afterwards to allow the probiotic strains to colonise your oral cavity. For optimal results, use daily before bed — this gives the beneficial bacteria the longest uninterrupted window to establish themselves.</p>",
            "category": "usage"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_ewnCBq": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "How long before I notice results?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long before I notice results?",
            "answer": "<p>Most users report fresher breath within the first 5–7 days. For noticeable improvements in oral comfort, consistent daily use for 4 to 8 weeks is typically needed. Your oral microbiome took years to become imbalanced; restoring it is a gradual process, not an overnight fix. Clinical studies on L. reuteri observed meaningful changes in gum-related markers at the 4-week mark.</p>",
            "category": "product"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_nhfxhT": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "What makes this different from gut probiotics?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What makes this different from gut probiotics?",
            "answer": "<p>Gut probiotics are encapsulated to survive stomach acid and colonise your intestines. OralBiome Pro is designed to dissolve in your mouth, delivering clinically studied bacterial strains directly to the oral cavity, where they're needed. The strains in our formula (L. reuteri, S. salivarius K12, S. salivarius M18) have been specifically researched for oral health benefits, not digestive ones.</p>",
            "category": "product"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_xapmVw": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "Can children use this product?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can children use this product?",
            "answer": "<p>OralBiome Pro is formulated for adults. Do not give to children who cannot safely dissolve a lozenge — choking risk applies to young children. For children over 12, consult a healthcare professional before use. The probiotic strains in our formula have been studied in paediatric populations with favourable safety profiles.</p>",
            "category": "product"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_pPGkWa": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "Can I use it alongside mouthwash?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use it alongside mouthwash?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, but timing matters. Use OralBiome Pro after mouthwash, never before. Antibacterial mouthwash can reduce the viability of the probiotic strains if used immediately after. We recommend waiting at least 30 minutes after mouthwash before dissolving your lozenge. Ideally, the best routine is: brush, floss, lozenge, sleep.</p>",
            "category": "usage"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_krnUdm": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "Do I need to refrigerate it?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need to refrigerate it?",
            "answer": "<p>No. OralBiome Pro is shelf-stable at room temperature below 25 degrees Celsius. Store in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight. The jar is designed to protect the probiotic strains from moisture. No special storage is needed. Keep it on your nightstand or in your bathroom cabinet.</p>",
            "category": "usage"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_3EXdBJ": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "Is it safe during pregnancy or breastfeeding?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is it safe during pregnancy or breastfeeding?",
            "answer": "<p>The strains in OralBiome Pro, particularly L. reuteri, have been used in clinical studies involving pregnant women without reported adverse effects. However, as with any food supplement during pregnancy or breastfeeding, we recommend consulting your healthcare provider before starting use. Your doctor knows your individual circumstances best.</p>",
            "category": "product"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_G3KkcX": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "How does the subscription work?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does the subscription work?",
            "answer": "<p>Your first jar ships immediately after ordering. Subsequent deliveries are automatic every 30 days, or 60 to 90 days if you prefer. You choose the frequency. You save 20% compared to one-time purchases. There are no commitments. You can skip a month, change your delivery frequency, or cancel entirely from your account dashboard with one click. No phone calls, no retention tricks, no penalties.</p>",
            "category": "subscription"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_qXyFhU": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "Can I pause or cancel my subscription?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I pause or cancel my subscription?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, instantly, anytime. Log in to your account at calqix.com, go to your subscription, and click pause or cancel. Changes take effect immediately. If you pause, your subscription resumes automatically after the skipped period. If you cancel, you will not be charged again. We also offer a 60-day money-back guarantee on your first order if you are not satisfied.</p>",
            "category": "product"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_tAbBm9": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "What clinical evidence supports this product?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What clinical evidence supports this product?",
            "answer": "<p>The primary strain in OralBiome Pro, Lactobacillus reuteri, has been researched in over 70 peer-reviewed clinical studies for oral health applications. These studies have explored its role in supporting gum health, maintaining oral microbiome balance, and contributing to overall oral comfort. S. salivarius K12 has been studied for over 30 years for its role in supporting fresh breath by helping maintain a balanced oral bacterial environment. We maintain a research page at calqix.com/research with direct links to published studies.</p>",
            "category": "product"
          }
        }
      },
